From ccfbe56fe609aa9b0906c707ba2ef1ea8c045ee0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emergent-agent-e1 <github@emergent.sh>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 09:12:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] iter164q: wire Campaign Composer to iter164p greeting +
 founder-badge fields
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Frontend-only. Backend iter164p already published (adds accepted campaign
fields `greeting: string | null` and `show_founder_badge: boolean | null`).

Composer changes (app/admin/campaigns/new/page.tsx):

  1. Editable Greeting / Addressee field
     - New input under Letter contents. Default value:
         'Dear [Contact name],'
     - Users can edit to anything ('Dear John,', 'Hello Mary,',
       'Hi there,') or clear the field entirely.
     - Empty string is a first-class value and means 'no greeting line'.
     - Hint text explains the [Contact name] placeholder semantics.

  2. Show Founding Member badge checkbox
     - New toggle under Letter contents.
     - Community / Outreach update default: OFF
     - Founding Member update default: ON

  3. Template switching updates BOTH defaults, but only when the
     current value still equals the *previous* template's default.
     A deliberately-edited greeting or a manually-flipped badge is
     preserved across a template switch.

  4. Draft load respects saved values verbatim, including saved
     empty greeting ("") and false badge — no silent restore of
     defaults on reopen.

  5. Save payload always forwards both fields (greeting always a
     string in state; showFounderBadge always a boolean).

  6. useEffect debounced-save deps updated so an edit to either
     new field triggers a draft save just like the existing fields.

Campaign type widened in lib/cms-api.ts to expose:
  greeting?:            string  | null
  show_founder_badge?:  boolean | null

Scope:
  - Only 2 files touched (app/admin/campaigns/new/page.tsx, lib/cms-api.ts).
  - No backend changes.
  - No changes to preview/send behaviour (backend iter164p handles
    both consistently already).
  - No changes to Campaign Composer edit-page details view or any
    other campaign / audience code path.

Build/typecheck: tsc --noEmit clean, next build ✓ Compiled successfully.
---
 app/admin/campaigns/new/page.tsx | 101 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 lib/cms-api.ts                   |  10 +++
 2 files changed, 110 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

